  "description": "Alpe d'Huez is the Oisans valley's flagship resort. Known for: the Sarenne (16km black run, longest in Europe), the 21-hairpin Tour de France road, and its 250km linked domain including Vaujany, Oz-en-Oisans, and Auris. The resort itself is purpose-built at 1,860m on a sun-exposed plateau. Two sectors: Pic Blanc (3,330m \u2014 glacier, Sarenne, off-piste) and Les Grandes Rousses (2,700m, wooded intermediate terrain). Family-friendly with excellent beginner zones.",
